Let \( S \) be a set with 2002 elements, and let \( N \) be an integer with \( 0 \leq N \leq 2^{2002} \). Prove that it is possible to color every subset of \( S \) either black or white so that the following conditions hold:
(a) the union of any two white subsets is white;
(b) the union of any two black subsets is black;
(c) there are exactly \( N \) white subsets.

The function is given by \( f(x)=a \ln x+1 \) where \( a > 0 \).
1. When \( x > 0 \), prove that \( f(x)-1 \geq a\left(1-\frac{1}{x}\right) \);
2. On the interval \( (1, \mathrm{e}) \), \( f(x) > x \) always holds. Find the range of the real number \( a \);
3. When \( a=\frac{1}{2} \), prove that \( f(2)+f(3)+\cdots+f(n+1) > 2(n + 1 - \sqrt{n+1}) \) for \( n \in \mathbb{N}^* \).

Prove that there exist infinitely many positive integers $n$, such that the $3n$ numbers $1, 2, \cdots, 3n$ can be arranged into a table:
$$
\begin{array}{llll}
a_{1} & a_{2} & \cdots & a_{n} \\
b_{1} & b_{2} & \cdots & b_{n} \\
c_{1} & c_{2} & \cdots & c_{n}
\end{array}
$$

satisfying the following conditions:
(1) $a_{1}+b_{1}+c_{1}=a_{2}+b_{2}+c_{2}=\cdots=a_{n}+b_{n}+c_{n}$, and it is a multiple of 6;
(2) $a_{1}+a_{2}+\cdots+a_{n}=b_{1}+b_{2}+\cdots+b_{n}=c_{1}+c_{2}+\cdots+c_{n}$, and it is a multiple of 6.

Let the domain and range of \( f(x) \) be the set of non-negative real numbers, and let \( f(x) \) satisfy the following conditions:
1. \( f(x \cdot f(y)) \cdot f(y) = f(x + y) \) for all \( x, y \geqslant 0 \);
2. \( f(2) = 0 \);
3. \( f(x) \neq 0 \) for all \( 0 \leqslant x < 2 \).

Find all functions \( f(x) \) that satisfy the above conditions.

If the equation $||x-2|-1|=a$ has three integer solutions for $x$, then what is the value of $a$?
(A) 0 ;
(B) 1 ;
(C) 2 ;
(D) 3 .
